    <title>Bounded gaps and perfect power gaps in sequences of consecutive primes</title>
    <updated>2026-02-07T14:06:18Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.07558v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.07558v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We study whether several consecutive prime gaps can all be
  relatively large at the same time, or is it possible that all are squares
  or perfect powers, or perhaps none of them are squares?
  A few related results and problems are also presented.</summary>
